# Build output and working tapes. Nothing here is truth: every byte is re-derivable by
#   build\build.cmd test
# and the receipts under receipts\ carry the numbers that were measured from them.
bin/
build/obj/
/scratch/
# NOT qc/scratch/ — those are the reviewers' probes and their outputs, which the QC reports cite as
# evidence. Their compiled binaries are excluded by the patterns below; their sources stay.

# Except for whole-file copies of OTHER projects that the reviewers took as working material:
# fusord.cpp (chunked) and the osv_* engine headers belong to their own codebases, and MIT-licensing
# them here would relicense those projects by accident. The QC reports quote them with line numbers
# where the argument needs it, which is the evidence; the whole files are not ours to publish.
qc/scratch/tape/chunk-*.md
qc/scratch/tape/INDEX.md
qc/scratch/tape/_manifest.json
qc/scratch/conv/
osv_*.cuh
osv_*.h
osv_core_test.cpp
osv_dispatch_test.cpp
qc/scratch/license/osv_dispatch_test
*.exe
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.tmp
# an ELF binary with no extension; the .cpp beside it is the evidence
# (git has no trailing comments on a pattern line — the whole line is the pattern)
qc/scratch/license/qc4_probe
